Z||000000||MooCow||09-24-2000||10:38 PM||||Okay well for a while now I have had a howling type noise and still can't seem to find it.  Now this time I got out of my car and I listen really closley and it sounds like air is being sucked in from that air intake on the side of the of the Fiero.  How can that be?  It is really loud and when you hit the gas it makes a higher pitch noise.  Nothing is in its way like a leaf so what could this noise be?  It's not the AC compressor nor should it be the altinator because it was changed less than 3 months ago.  Anyone have a clue what to look for?? <BR>Also the air filter makes a noise like air is just spiining in there.  I replaced the air filter with a KN a while ago and it didnt clear it up.  what to do??<P>                               Thanks Ken<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by MooCow (edited 09-24-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||stsmithgt||09-25-2000||03:34 PM||||oops. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 09-25-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||stsmithgt||09-25-2000||03:35 PM||||I have had a similar problem.  It sounded like a bad vacume leak whistle.  It turned out to be the gasket underneath the air filter housing.  Why it sucked so loud through there I don't know.  Maybe my intake through the body panel is too restricted.  The paper gasket was wasted though.  I made one out of some rubber that would seal it up better and the noise went away.  I think I need to take a better look at it.  Getting rid of the symptom doesn't mean I fixed the problem. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Good luck with your noise.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">   ||||reg||10
Z||000003||theogre||09-25-2000||08:32 PM||||could be the gaskets like said above. could just be allot of turbulance. Most of the V6's I've heard make a racket in the intake ducts.||||reg||1
